$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Solutions of ester (0.2 M in toluene, prepared
in a screw-cap volumetric flask, under argon), DIBALH (1 M in toluene)
and methanol (neat) were loaded into syringes and introduced to the
system using syringe pumps set to the appropriate flow rates. After a
steady state was reached the mixture exiting the system was collected and
then treated with a saturated aqueous solution of Rochelle's salt,
diluted with diethyl ether and stirred until 2 clear phases were
obtained. The organic phase was then analyzed by GC. 5d, yield 98%.
[α]24D -5.5 (c 1.9, CHCl3)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM flow system, ester flow rate 5 mL/min, DIBALH flow rate 2 mL/min,
optimization study (optimized on reactor length, reactor inner diameter,
ester flow rate, DIBALH flow rate, reaction temperature and reaction
time), other products also detected (1% of the alcohol)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diisobutylaluminum Hydride Reductions Revitalized: A Fast, Robust, and
Selective Continuous Flow System for Aldehyde Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Webb, Damien; Jamison, Timothy F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(2), 568-571

