atmosphere. After stirring at -78°C for 15 min, S22 (510 mg, 3.00 mmol)
was added dropwise to the mixture at -78°C, and stirred at -78°C for 30
min. Triethylamine (3.9 ml, 27.9 mmol) was added dropwise to the mixture
at -78°C, and stirred at rt for 1.5 h. The reaction was quenched with
aqueous NH4Cl. The organic phase was extracted with CH2Cl2, and dried
over anhydrous MgSO4. Silica gel column chromatography (10% EtOAc/Hexane)
of crude product gave S23. (429 mg, 2.55 mmol, 85%) as a colorless oil:
1H-NMR (400 MHz/CDCl3) δ 9.50 (s, 1H), 5.51 (dt, J = 11.4, 7.6 Hz, 1H),
5.27 (dt, J = 11.4, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 1.91 (ddt, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.6 Hz, 2H),
1.32-1.22 (m, 6H), 1.20 (s, 6H), 0.87 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H); 13C-NMR (100
MHz/CDCl3) δ 203.28, 134.78, 131.29, 47.60, 31.39, 29.36, 28.50, 23.19
(2C), 22.48, 13.96; ESI-MS (m/z) 169.4 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
