$DATUM (6R, 4S) and (6R, 4R)-4-Cyano-6-(2-phenylethyl)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxane
(6). A solution of ester 1s (698 mg, 2.37 mmol) was dissolved in Et2O (6
mL), transferred to a 50 mL flask and cooled to -78 °C. DIBALH (2.8 mL of
a 1.0 M solution in toluene) was added dropwise. The resulting solution
was maintained for 1 h and then the reaction was quenched with 200 μL
ethyl formate. The reaction solution was transferred via cannula to a
chilled (0 °C) solution of 1 M sodium potassium tartrate (30 mL) and the
biphasic mixture was stirred vigorously for 30 minutes. The aqueous phase
was extracted with Et2O (3 x 30 mL). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (30 mL), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vacuo to a
colorless oil. The oil was filtered through a plug of SiO2 (10:90
Et2O:hexanes) to give the corresponding aldehyde as a colorless oil,
yield 471 mg, 79%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
