$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General method for the synthesis of aldehyde derivatives. The methyl
ester was dissolved in distilled diethyl ether (0.2 M) and the resulting
solution was placed under a nitrogen atmosphere. This solution and
diisobutyl aluminium hydride (DIBAL) (3 equiv) in diethyl ether (0.6 M)
was cooled in a -78 °C acetone-dry ice bath. The DIBAL solution was
cannula transferred to the methyl ester solution and the solution was
stirred for 1 h. At -78 °C, methanol (equal to half of the diethyl ether
by volume) was added, and then 15 equiv of acetic acid was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 5 min and then transferred to an ice
bath, and saturated sodium tartrate solution (equal to the volume of
diethyl ether) was added. After the mixture was stirred in the ice-bath
for 20 min, the mixture was transferred to a separatory funnel and ethyl
actetate and water were added. The aqueous layer was extracted three
times with ethyl acetate. The organic washes were combined and extracted
once with water. The organic layer was dried with anhydrous sodium
sulfate and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The product
was purified by reverse phase preparatory HPLC (5 to 95% acetonitrile
over 50 min). The compound above (14.8 mg, 0.042 mmol, 22%) was prepared
from 75 mg (0.19 mmol) of the corresponding methyl ester and 0.10 mL
(0.58 mmol) of DIBAL according to the procedure above. The NMR data
corresponds to the hydrated product for a mixture of diastereomers. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, 3:1 CD3CN:D2O): δ 0.72-1.29 (m, 13), 1.74 (m, 3), 1.84-1.95
(m, 2), 2.42-2.53 (m, 1), 4.35-4.40 (m, 1), 5.10 (d, 0.77, J = 5.2), 5.12
(d, 0.23, J = 5.2), 7.43 (app. t, 2, J = 7.4), 7.51 (t, 1, J = 7.4), 7.71
(d, 2, J = 3.6), 7.78 (s, 0.73), 7.81 (s, 0.27). About 5% of the aldehyde
product was observable. HRMS (FAB+) m/z: 357.2290 (MH+ C20H29N4O2
requires 357.2291).
