$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General method for the synthesis of aldehyde
derivatives. The methyl ester was dissolved in distilled diethyl ether
(0.2 M) and the resulting solution was placed under a nitrogen
atmosphere. This solution and diisobutyl aluminium hydride (DIBAL) (3
equiv) in diethyl ether (0.6 M) was cooled in a -78 °C acetone-dry ice
bath. The DIBAL solution was cannula transferred to the methyl ester
solution and the solution was stirred for 1 h. At -78 °C, methanol (equal
to half of the diethyl ether by volume) was added, and then 15 equiv of
acetic acid was added. The reaction mixture was stirred for 5 min and
then transferred to an ice bath, and saturated sodium tartrate solution
(equal to the volume of diethyl ether) was added. After the mixture was
stirred in the ice-bath for 20 min, the mixture was transferred to a
separatory funnel and ethyl actetate and water were added. The aqueous
layer was extracted three times with ethyl acetate. The organic washes
were combined and extracted once with water. The organic layer was dried
with anhydrous sodium sulfate and the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. The product was purified by reverse phase preparatory HPLC (5
to 95% acetonitrile over 50 min). The compound above (5.1 mg, 0.013 mmol,
18%) was prepared from 30 mg (0.073 mmol) of the corresponding methyl
ester and 39 μM (0.22 mmol) of DIBAL according to the procedure above.
The NMR data corresponds to the hydrated product for a mixture of
diastereomers. 1H NMR (500 MHz, 3:1 CD3CN:D2O): δ 0.70-0.93 (m, 10),
1.03-1.31 (m, 3), 1.73-1.81 (m, 3), 1.81-1.92 (m, 2), 2.27-2.36 (m, 1),
3.98 (s, 3), 4.34-4.42 (m, 1), 5.07-5.11 (m, 0.67), 5.11-5.15 (m, 0.33),
7.00-7.08 (m, 1), 7.08-7.17 (m, 1), 7.41-7.53 (m, 1), 7.68-7.72 (m,
0.58), 7.72-7.78 (m, 0.42), 7.80-7.88 (m, 1). About 5% of the aldehyde
product was observable. HRMS (FAB+) m/z: 405.2501 (MH+ of the hydrate,
C21H33N4O4 requires 405.2502).
