$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The methyl ester (48 mg, 0.12 mmol, 1 equiv) was dissolved in 0.54 mL of
distilled diethyl ether and put under a nitrogen atmosphere. This
solution and diisobutyl aluminium hydride (DIBAL) (57 μL, 0.32 mmol, 3
equiv) in 0.54 mL of diethyl ether was cooled in a -78 °C acetone-dry ice
bath. The DIBAL solution was cannula transferred to the methyl ester
solution and the solution was stirred for 1 h. At -78 °C, methanol (equal
to half of the diethyl ether by volume) was added, and then 15 equiv of
acetic acid was added. The reaction solution was stirred for 5 min and
then transferred to an ice bath, and a saturated sodium tartrate solution
(equal to the volume of diethyl ether) was added. After the reaction
solution was stirred in the ice-bath for 20 min, the reaction solution
was transferred to a separatory funnel, and ethyl actetate (25 mL) and
water (5 mL) was added. The aqueous layer was extracted three times with
ethyl acetate (25 mL). The organic washes were combined and extracted
once with water (15 mL). The organic layer was dried with anhydrous
sodium sulfate and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The
product was purified by reverse phase preparatory HPLC (5 to 95%
acetonitrile over 50 min). The NMR data corresponds to the hydrated
product for a mixture of diastereomers. 1H NMR (500 MHz, 3:1 CD3CN:D2O):
δ 0.70-0.95 (m, 10), 1.12-1.32 (m, 3), 1.69-1.76 (m, 3), 1.83-2.00 (m,
2), 2.45-2.54 (m, 1), 4.36-4.45 (m, 1), 5.11 (d, 0.75, J = 5.4), 5.13 (d,
0.25, J = 5.1), 7.30-7.45 (m, 2), 7.82 (s, 0.72), 7.85 (s, 0.28),
7.90-8.00 (m, 1). About 5% of the aldehyde product was observable. HRMS
(FAB+) m/z: 363.1850 (MH+ C18H29N4O3S requires 363.1855).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
