$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Solutions of ester (0.2 M in toluene, prepared in a screw-cap volumetric
flask, under argon), DIBALH (1 M in toluene) and methanol (neat) were
loaded into syringes and introduced to the system using syringe pumps set
to the appropriate flow rates. After a steady state was reached the
mixture exiting the system was collected and then treated with a
saturated aqueous solution of Rochelle's salt, diluted with diethyl ether
and stirred until 2 clear phases were obtained. The organic phase was
then analyzed by GC. Final prodcuct.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM flow system, ester flow rate 30 mL/min, DIBALH flow rate 6 mL/min,
optimization study (optimized on reactor length, reactor inner diameter,
ester flow rate, DIBALH flow rate, reaction temperature and reaction
time)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Diisobutylaluminum Hydride Reductions Revitalized: A Fast, Robust, and
Selective Continuous Flow System for Aldehyde Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Webb, Damien; Jamison, Timothy F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(2), 568-571

