$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2S,3S)/(2R,3R)-tert-butyl
2-(bis(tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino)-3-methyl-5-oxopentanoate, S10
(2S,3S)/(2R,3R)-tert-Butyl
2-(di-tert-butoxycarbonyl-amino)-3-methyl-4-methoxy-4-oxobutanoate S7 (45
mg, 0.11 mmol) was dissolved in dry diethyl ether (3 mL). The solution
was cooled down to -78 °C under nitrogen atmosphere before addition of 1
M diisobutyl aluminum hydride solution in tetrahydrofuran (0.09 mL, 0.8
eq.) and stirring for 90 min. Another 0.8 eq. of DIBAL-H solution was
added and after 90 additional min under those conditions, the reaction
was quenched with water (0.05 mL) and allowed to reach room temperature
over 30 min. The precipitate was filtered through a pad of Celite® 545,
washed with diethyl ether and the filtrate was evaporated to give a
colorless oil which was purified using silica chromatography (SNAP-10
column, gradient elution with 0-100% ethyl acetate in hexane) to give the
pure (2S,3S)/(2R,3R)-tert-butyl 2-(bis(tertbutoxycarbonyl)
amino)-3-methyl-5-oxopentanoate S10 and the undesired alcohol
(2S,3S)/(2R,3R)-tert-butyl 2-(bis(tert-butoxycarbonyl)-
amino)-5-hydroxy-3-methylpentanoate. Yield 37 mg, 80%, colorless oil;
yield 9 mg, 20%, white solid. Aldehyde S10: TLC: 1:1 hexane/EtOAc, Rf =
0.65. IR (neat) ν/cm-1: 1741 (OC=O), 1699 (NC=O). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 9.71-9.69 (m, 1H), 4.52 (dd, J = 9.0, 3.0, 1H), 3.00-2.90 (m,
1H), 2.51-2.45 (m, 1H), 2.25-2.17 (m, 1H), 1.51 (s, 18H), 1.45 (s, 9H),
1.16 (dd, J = 6.5, 3.0, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 201.9, 168.6,
152.7, 83.2, 81.5, 62.7, 47.4, 28.6, 27.9 (2x), 19.6. LR ESI-MS: 424.23
([M+Na]+), 825.46 ([2M+Na]+). Alcohol: mp 77-79 °C. TLC: 1:1
hexane/EtOAc, Rf = 0.45. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.43 (dd, J = 9.0,
3.0, 1H), 3.76-3.69 (m, 1H), 3.66-3.59 (m, 1H), 2.49-2.41 (m, 1H),
1.70-1.61 (m, 1H), 1.59 (bs, 1H), 1.50 (s, 18H), 1.43 (s, 9H), 1.38-1.26
(m, 1H), 1.11 (dd, J = 6.5, 3.0, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
169.2, 152.8, 82.9, 81.1, 63.5, 60.6, 35.4, 29.6, 28.0, 27.9, 18.8. LR
ESI-MS: 426.23 ([M+Na]+), 829.42 ([2M+Na]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of DIBAL-H after 90 minutes in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Crotonase Catalysis Enables Flexible Production of Functionalized
Prolines and Carbapenams
