$DATUM (2S,3R)/(2R,3S)-tert-butyl
2-(bis(tert-butoxycarbonyl)amino)-3-methyl-5-oxopentanoate, S11
(2S,3R)/(2R,3S)-tert-Butyl
2-(di-tert-butoxycarbonyl-amino)-3-methyl-4-methoxy-4-oxobutanoate S9 (30
mg, 0.07 mmol) was dissolved in dry diethyl ether (2 mL). The solution
was cooled down to -78 °C under nitrogen atmosphere before addition of 1
M diisobutyl aluminum hydride solution in hexanes (0.21 mL, 3.0 eq.).
After stirring for 90 min, the reaction was quenched with water (0.1 mL)
and allowed to reach room temperature over 30 min. The aluminum hydroxide
precipitate was filtered off through a pad of Celite® 545, washed with
diethyl ether and the filtrate was evaporated to give a colorless oil
which was purified using silica chromatography (SNAP-10 column, gradient
elution with 0-50% ethyl acetate in hexane) to give the pure
(2S,3R)/(2R,3S)-tert-butyl 2-(bis(tertbutoxycarbonyl)
amino)-3-methyl-5-oxopentanoate S11 and the undesired alcohol
(2S,3R)/(2R,3S)-tert-butyl 2-(bis(tert-butoxycarbonyl)-
amino)-5-hydroxy-3-methylpentanoate. Yield 23 mg, 80%, colorless oil;
yield 6 mg, 19%, colorless oil. Aldehyde S11: TLC: 8:2 hexane/EtOAc, Rf =
0.40. IR (neat) ν/cm-1: 1743 (OC=O), 1701 (NC=O). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 9.77 (d, J = 2.0, 1H), 4.54 (d, J = 9.5, 1H), 2.99-2.94 (m,
2H), 2.47 (ddd, J = 17.5, 9.5, 2.5, 1H), 1.52 (s, 18H), 1.44 (s, 9H),
0.91 (d, J = 7.0, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 201.6, 169.1, 152.6,
83.0, 81.6, 61.8, 50.0, 28.0, 27.9, 16.7. HR ESI-MS: 424.2306 ([M+Na]+,
C20H35NNaO7+, calc. 424.2306).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Crotonase Catalysis Enables Flexible Production of Functionalized
Prolines and Carbapenams
