$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7S-Isopropyl-4R-methyloxepan-2S-ol (5a) and
6S-Hydroxy-3R,7-dimethyloctanal (5b). A solution of (-)-menthone lactone
(1, 2.00 g, 11.8 mmol) that was prepared from l-menthol according to the
literature [2] in anhydrous THF (40 mL) at 70°C was treated dropwise with
a solution (73%) of DIBAH (3.0 mL, 12.0 mmol) in toluene. After the
lactone was fully converted (15 min, TLC), the mixture was poured onto
ice (10 mL), diluted with t-BuOMe (50 mL), filtered through a layer of
Al2O3 (5 cm), dried over MgSO4, and evaporated to afford a 1:1 mixture of
lactol (5a) and hydroxyaldehyde (5b). The PMR and 13C NMR parameters of
5a and 5b were identical to those reported previously [4]. Yield 1.93 g,
98%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
