$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Batch Reactions. All experiments were carried out in a 500 mL jacketed
vessel equipped with a mechanical stirrer. A 20% Dibal-H solution in
toluene (1.0 equiv) was added over 20 min to a 2.3% methyl butyrate
solution in toluene at the temperature indicated in Table 1. The reaction
mixture was then directly poured into a 2 M aqueous hydrochloric acid
solution at 20 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM ER-25 microreactor with mass flow controller used, close to 90%
selectivity on target butyraldehyde obtained, continuous flow,
optimization study, optimized on microreactor type, temperature, other
product also detected, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dibal-H Reduction of Methyl Butyrate into Butyraldehyde using
Microreactors
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ducry, Laurent; Roberge, Dominique M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2008), 12(2), 163-167

