$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4R*,4aS*,8aR*)-4-Hydroxymethyl-2-methyl-8a-vinyl-1,4,4a,5,8,8a-hexahydro-2H-isoquinolin-3-one
and
(4S*,4aS*,8aR*)-4-Hydroxymethyl-2-methyl-8a-vinyl-1,4,4a,5,8,8a-hexahydro-2H-isoquinolin-3-one.
Oxalyl chloride (240 μL, 2.75 mmol) was added dropwise to a slurry of
octahydroisoquinoline-4-carboxylicAcid derivatives (320 mg, 1.36 mmol) in
benzene (6.8 mL) and the mixture was stirred for 5 h. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure (water aspirator with drying tube), the
residue was redissolved in benzene (6 mL) and the solution was
concentrated. The resulting green residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (6.8mL)
and the solution was immediately cooled to -78 °C. Diisobutylaluminum
hydride (1.5 mL of a 1.0 M solution in toluene, 1.5 mmol) was added
dropwise and the solution was warmed to 0 °C over 1.5 h. The solution was
returned to -78 °C and an additional 1.1 equiv of diisobutylaluminum
hydride (1.5 mL of a 1.0 M solution in toluene, 1.5 mmol) was added
dropwise. The solution was warmed to 0 °C over 1 h and then cooled to -78
°C as EtOAc (0.5 mL) was added to quench excess hydride reagent. After 5
min, the cold bath was removed and Rochelle's salt solution (10%, 20 mL)
was added. The mixture was stirred vigorously for 4 h and extracted with
CH2Cl2 (4 x 20 mL). The combined extracts were dried (Na2SO4), filtered,
concentrated, and purified by flash column chromatography (1:1 hexanes :
EtOAc to EtOAc, 20 g silica) to give 35 mg 11% of an aldehyde as a solid,
16 mg 4% of an isobutyl ester as a pale yellow oil,
(4R*,4aS*,8aR*)-4-Hydroxymethyl-2-methyl-8a-vinyl-1,4,4a,5,8,8a-hexahydro-2H-isoquinolin-3-one
as pale yellow oil, yield 22 mg 7% and
(4S*,4aS*,8aR*)-4-Hydroxymethyl-2-methyl-8a-vinyl-1,4,4a,5,8,8a-hexahydro-2H-isoquinolin-3-one
as a colorless crystalline solid, yield 124 mg 48%.
(4R*,4aS*,8aR*)-4-Hydroxymethyl-2-methyl-8a-vinyl-1,4,4a,5,8,8a-hexahydro-2H-isoquinolin-3-one:
Rf 0.28 (EtOAc); mp 96-97 °C; IR (neat) 3395, 3023, 2919, 2846, 1635,
1506, 1457, 1437, 1326, 1251, 1048 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.69
(dd, J = 17.6, 11.2 Hz, 1H), 5.70 - 5.64 (m, 1H), 5.57 - 5.50 (m, 1H),
5.16 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.13 (d, J = 17.6 Hz, 1H), 4.43 - 4.32 (m,
1H), 3.84 (d, J = 10.4 Hz, 1H), 3.67 (dd, J = 10.8, 8.4 Hz, 1H), 3.34 (d,
J = 12.8 Hz, 1H), 2.95 (s, 3H), 2.84 (d, J = 12.4 Hz, 1H), 2.39 (ddd, J =
11.6, 8.4, 3.2 Hz, 1H), 2.33- 2.23 (m, 1H), 2.23 - 2.14 (m, 1H), 2.05 -
1.94 (m, 2H), 1.71 (dd, J = 10.8. 5.2 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
172.9, 141.3, 124.1, 124.0, 114.8, 63.6, 58.6, 43.2, 37.2, 35.8, 34.9,
27.7, 25.9; MS (FAB) 222 (94), 220 (9), 204 (7), 155 (16), 154 (100);
HRMS m/e calc for C13H20NO2 (M + H+) 222.1494, found 222.1500.
(4S*,4aS*,8aR*)-4-Hydroxymethyl-2-methyl-8a-vinyl-1,4,4a,5,8,8a-hexahydro-2H-isoquinolin-3-one
Rf 0.44 (EtOAc); IR (neat) 3416, 3082, 3023, 2917, 2849, 1618, 1506,
1436, 1229, 1040, 914 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.76 (dd, J = 17.6,
10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.71 - 5.64 (m, 1H), 5.61 - 5.54 (m, 1H), 5.20 (d, J = 10.8
Hz, 1H), 5.06 (d, J = 17.6 Hz, 1H), 4.35 (d, J = 11.6 Hz, 1H), 3.93 (dd,
J = 10.4, 10.4 Hz, 1H), 3.55 (d, J = 12.8 Hz, 1H), 3.50 - 3.45 (m, 1H),
3.13 (dd, J = 12.0, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 2.95 (s, 3H), 2.75 (ddd, J = 8.8, 3.6,
3.6 Hz, 1H), 2.27 - 1.94 (m, 5H), 1.85 - 1.71 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 172.7, 143.6, 124.8, 123.8, 113.8, 63.8, 51.1, 43.9, 37.9, 36.8,
34.9, 34.1, 24.6; MS (CI) 222 (100), 221 (89), 220 (32), 205 (29), 191
(28), 165 (28); HRMS m/e calc for C13H19NO2 (M+) 221.1416, found
221.1421.
